 officials say there was clearly  a failure because the attackers passed  through several checkpoints controlled  by the taliban or afghan forces before  reaching the airport gates and u.s  troops  now to the story of an afghan who worked  as a special ops translator and now  lives in las vegas he has been working  to get his wife out of afghanistan and  to america safely in the meantime she  has been hiding from the taliban that is  why we're protecting their identity in  this story kirsten joyce tells us how  she's making it out  she is safe words h.k has been waiting  to share since i first met him two weeks  ago 15 days that i haven't had  probably no more than two hours  of sleep at night h.k lives in las vegas  where he became a u.s citizen last year  he and his wife got married in  afghanistan and he's been working for a  year to supply her with the proper  documents to come to the states  after the taliban takeover he was scared  for his wife's life she had to hide out  just 10 minutes from the airport in  kabul there was times of over 9 000  people around the airport it was a  humanitarian disaster hk worked day and  night with a variety of contacts to get  her safely to the airport folks he met  through his time as a translator helping  the u.s military in afghanistan for  nearly a decade his journey and efforts  being documented by his friend brian  johnson a guy who speaks five languages  that's beloved by the us military by  special forces that has worked with our  troops on the ground and loves this  country and now just wants to support  his community hk shared this photo with  us of his wife and brother-in-law when  they receive news they would be safely  leaving afghanistan on monday  they are now in kuwait last i heard from  the  embassy in kuwait the u.s embassy to say  that they're being processed and uh  once they're uh once they're getting  ready to take off from there and they'll  uh possibly send me you know a  description of the flight itinerary  where they're going bring them here  bring them to the you know where i am so  hopefully that happens i'll go see her  wherever she lands in the united states  and we'll go from there it's funny he  thinks he's going by himself that's cute  although his wife and brother-in-law are  out of harm's way hk says his mission is  far from over my wife she's out of the  danger zone and i am focused on saving  everybody else kyrsten joyce 8 news now  h.k and bryant are currently in north  carolina hoping hk's wife lands there  but if not they'll go to wherever she's  flown hk has lived in las vegas for  eight years his mother and father also  live here will bring you the reunion of  course when he gets to embrace his wife  on u.s soil  up next on politics now a key date where  several unemployment programs will end  is just a few weeks away
 

